<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared merge train, as a consumer keeps it in
.github/workflows/merge-train.yml. The rendered file is the whole of the
consumer's train: the steps live in .github/workflows/merge-train.yml of the
shared repository, named here by commit with the version as a comment
(decision record 0029).

Before the first run: the merge-train app is installed on the repository, the
repository (or its organisation) holds the app's private key as the secret
MERGE_TRAIN_APP_KEY and its client id as the variable
MERGE_TRAIN_APP_CLIENT_ID. Without them the token step fails and the run is
red; nothing is written.

Off switch: the variable MERGE_TRAIN set to `off` makes every run report only.
Unset, the train runs.

Scopes: none. The called job writes with the app's token, minted per run for
this repository only; GITHUB_TOKEN gets no permission.

Required check: none. The job runs on a push to the default branch, on a
schedule and by hand, never on a pull request, and is no check of a pull
request (cordanaLLM/praetor#1212 for the name the engine declares).

Triggers: a push to the default branch is the moment the previous pull request
landed, so the next one moves at once; the hourly schedule, off the top of the
hour, picks up a pull request that turned clean without a push; dispatch is the
manual nudge. Concurrency keeps one run at a time and never cancels a run
halfway.

Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit and .Shared.Version are working
names until the engine renders caller templates (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211);
.RunnerTag is the engine's own.
*/ -%>
---
# Merge train: lands this repository's clean pull requests one at a time and
# keeps the next one up to date. The job is the shared workflow of
# <% .Shared.Repository %>, named by commit.
name: Merge train

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  schedule:
    - cron: "41 * * * *"
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: merge-train
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  train:
    name: Merge train
    permissions: {}
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/merge-train.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>
      app_client_id: ${{ vars.MERGE_TRAIN_APP_CLIENT_ID }}
      switch: ${{ vars.MERGE_TRAIN || 'on' }}
    secrets:
      app_private_key: ${{ secrets.MERGE_TRAIN_APP_KEY }}
